@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.4.2
@changelog
  - Codename: Reticulating Splines
  - Metering: the UF8's second gain-reduction row now shows the focused track's SSL gate attenuation (it was dark), in lock-step with the UC1 gate LEDs. Gate GR on both surfaces follows the selected track's channel strip instead of whichever SSL instance connected first.
  - Load: no more load-time track-selection countdown. With gate metering on, opening a project used to select track 14 down to 2, one per second, over ~12s; the plug-ins now connect in a quick burst so the selection settles almost instantly. Metering unaffected.
  - Nav Mode: top-soft-key marker/region jumps now work when a pinned startup soft-key bank (or any user-Quick) is engaged — the overlay owns the soft-keys while showing. Region jumps also work with the transport stopped. Uncoloured markers/regions are no longer dim on the UC1.
  - Soft-keys: FX dynamic-bank keys are colour-coded by SSL class (CS yellow / BC red / UF8 blue / plain white); a fixed startup soft-key bank can be pinned in Settings -> General.
